   "family": "motër",
   "is_root": true,
   "etymology": "First attested in 1555 by Buzuku using two forms: motrë and motërë. If motrë is the archaic form, then it can be reconstructed as Proto-Albanian *mā́terā- (“sister; having the same mother”). If motërë is the archaic form, then a Proto-Albanian *mā́teran could be reconstructed, from an older *mā́terān. Ultimately from from Proto-Indo-European *máh₂terah₂- (“woman/sister having the same mother”).\nAlternatively, from Proto-Albanian *mā́trā-, from Pre-Proto-Albanian *hmā́trā-, from Proto-Indo-European *smah₂tráh₂-, a simplified form of Proto-Indo-European *sm̥-mah₂tráh₂- (“from a common womb”).\nHistorically considered to be directly from Proto-Indo-European *méh₂tēr (“mother”), with the unusual explanation of the sister assuming the roles of the mother, though this would be a difficult explanation for such a change to occur language-wide.",
   "etymology_class": "inherited",
   "source_lang": null,
