   "is_root": true,
   "etymology": "* From Proto-Albanian *driktā, from Proto-Indo-European *dŕ̥ḱtis (“sight, vision; appearance”) + *-éh₂ (thematic feminine ending), from the root *derḱ- (“to see”). Cognate with Sanskrit दृष्टि (dṛ́ṣṭi, “sight, vision, aspect”) and Avestan 𐬛𐬀𐬭𐬱𐬙𐬌𐬯 (darštis, “sight”); further compare Old English torht (“clear, bright”) from the same root.\n* From Proto-Albanian *drit(t)a- < earlier *dritˢtā- < Proto-Indo-European *dŕ̥ḱtó- (“visible, bright”), from the root *derḱ- (“to see”).",
